      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early shipbuilding and whaling thrived in Mattapoisett Harbor, making Rochester a bustling maritime hub in its early years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1852 and 1857, the towns of Marion and Mattapoisett split off, leaving Rochester landlocked within Plymouth County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Mattapoisett and Sippican rivers run through Rochester, emptying into Buzzards Bay and shaping the town’s coastal landscape.",
